WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.467
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:05.400
You're here. You made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.267
Thank you for watching.
This is very exciting.

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:10.834
The 46th President of
the United States, Joe Biden,

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:12.334
is my guest tonight.

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:14.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.534
You know you have a crazy job
when you're meeting

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:23.934
with Vladimir Putin and me
in the same week, you know?

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.934
That's right -- President Biden
is here to discuss

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:27.934
the economy,
his infrastructure bill,

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:29.767
and break down the first two
episodes of

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:32.000
the "Sex and the City" reboot.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.033
What happened to Samantha?

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:37.567
The president was
actually supposed to be here

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.868
earlier this week,
but he had to lay low after

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:42.267
he lit the Fox News
Christmas tree on fire.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:43.267
And...

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:44.734
Yeah.

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:48.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:54.334
Before the show,
I asked President Biden

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:57.133
how excited he is to be
with us on a scale of 1-10.

00:00:57.133 --> 00:01:00.434
And he said, "10,
but 6 without inflation."

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:02.300
I thought it was...

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.467
Biden's got a busy day.

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:05.434
Besides talking to us,
he's also talking to

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:08.434
the National Guard
to prep for SantaCon.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:11.300
Here's some good news.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.400
I saw that jobless claims
have dropped to

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:16.067
the lowest level in 52 years.

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:18.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:24.200
Is that how you wanted me
to say it, Mr. President?

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:29.901
That's right --
everyone's working.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:31.133
In fact,
for the first time ever,

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.501
contestants on "The Bachelor"

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:35.100
don't have to make up
a fake job.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.868
"I'm a personal trainer,
entrepreneur,

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:38.901
social-media coach."

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.734
Well, here in
New York City tomorrow,

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:45.400
thousands of people will pack
the streets for SantaCon.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.100
Or, as the NYPD calls it,

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.367
"The Nightmare
Before Christmas."

00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:51.734
That's right --
starting tomorrow at 10:00 a.m.,

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:53.067
bartenders will be handing out

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:56.734
more shots than
a CVS pharmacist.

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:57.968
That's right -- SantaCon is

00:01:57.968 --> 00:01:59.501
officially back
in New York City.

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:01.234
It was canceled last year,
but this weekend,

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:03.200
thousands of people
dressed like Santa

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.734
are expected to take part in
a citywide bar crawl.

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:10.367
So I thought I'd welcome the
tradition back with a tiny song.

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:13.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.667
Thank you.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.501
♪♪

00:02:18.501 --> 00:02:22.968
♪ Christmas in New York
is for you, and it's for me ♪

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:25.667
♪ And a couple of thousand
drunken Santas

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:27.767
stumbling down the street ♪

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:30.100
♪ With pillows
stuffed under red shirts,

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.434
the most I ever saw ♪

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:34.434
♪ Fake white beards
and Christmas cheer

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:36.300
and cases of White Claw ♪

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:39.567
♪♪

00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:41.701
♪ But they don't got
no reindeer ♪

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:43.901
♪ No cocoa piping hot ♪

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:46.200
♪ Just snowstorms
of Axe Body Spray ♪

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.400
♪ And dollar Jell-O shots ♪

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.567
♪ There's Santas on the subway ♪

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:53.100
♪ There's Santas taking naps ♪

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.000
♪ One Santa is break-dancing ♪

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.501
♪ One's barfing in his hat ♪

00:02:57.501 --> 00:02:59.767
♪ Some are singing carols ♪

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:01.767
♪ Some say "ho, ho, ho" ♪

00:03:01.767 --> 00:03:04.334
♪ But most of them
are running, shouting,

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:06.434
"Look out, bro! Po-po!"

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:07.567
♪ One drunk Santa,

00:03:07.567 --> 00:03:08.701
two drunk Santa ♪

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:10.701
♪ Three drunk Santa, four ♪

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:15.200
♪ I saw Santa kiss Green M&amp;M
at the M&amp;M store ♪

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.400
♪ So get your booster,
wear a mask,

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.734
be safe this SantaCon ♪

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:21.734
♪ 'Cause beer and milk
and cookies

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.534
don't protect from Omicron ♪

00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:26.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:27.667
Thank you.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.567
Thank you, Roots.

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:34.868
Some entertainment news.

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:36.234
Steven Spielberg's

00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:38.834
"West Side Story"
hit theaters today.

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:40.400
Yeah. Some people said,
if they want to watch

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.033
a heartbreaking story
about the Jets,

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:44.067
they should just watch football.

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:48.100
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.434
Well, this is fun.

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:52.067
Margaritaville just announced
its own cruise line

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:55.567
that will start sailing
out of Florida in the spring.

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.868
A Margaritaville cruise
out of Florida.

00:03:57.868 --> 00:04:00.267
What could possibly go right?

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:02.834
But it sounds pretty cool.

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:06.234
They even line the hot-tub rims
with margarita salt.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.968
And, finally,
the state of Delaware

00:04:08.968 --> 00:04:11.567
is replacing a highway exit sign
after they realized

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:14.467
the original one had
a small typo in "Delaware."

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:16.400
They left out one of the A's.
Take a look at this.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:19.100
Delware Avenue, yeah.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.667
Let's see the sign again
after they added the "A."

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:24.667
Delwarea Avenue.
There you go.

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.267
When he saw that,
President Biden

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:28.200
grabbed the ladder and said,
"I'll fix it myself."

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.400
We have a great show.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.801
Guys, we have
exactly six shows left before

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:33.634
we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time for

00:04:33.634 --> 00:04:35.367
that beloved
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:37.968
It's time for "12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters."

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:39.434
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:41.834
♪ 12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters ♪

00:04:41.834 --> 00:04:46.267
♪ Six days left ♪

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:47.434
-That is right.

00:04:47.434 --> 00:04:50.033
Every show
between now and Christmas,

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.234
we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:04:52.234 --> 00:04:54.501
a stunning
Christmas sweater from the

00:04:54.501 --> 00:04:56.067
Countdown to Christmas Cabinet.

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:57.901
Now, since there are
six shows left,

00:04:57.901 --> 00:05:00.934
let's open door number 6.

00:05:00.934 --> 00:05:03.234
[ Drumroll ]

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:04.400
Whenever you're ready.

00:05:05.634 --> 00:05:07.334
Alright.
♪♪

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:10.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.400
I don't understand.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:15.634
I don't quite -- Wow!

00:05:15.634 --> 00:05:17.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:18.934
Wow!

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:20.400
Oh, and it -- Turn it.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.834
So, it comes
with a hat on the back.

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:26.667
-Whoo!

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:28.667
-You can't wear it.
You can't wear it.

00:05:28.667 --> 00:05:30.167
It's stuck to the sweater.
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:30.167 --> 00:05:33.234
-Interesting. That's an
interesting way to do it.

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:35.501
Now let's see who's going to go
home with tonight's sweater.

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:36.901
Everyone look
at your seat number.

00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:38.334
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:39.767
Quest,
can I get a drumroll, please?

00:05:39.767 --> 00:05:40.868
Who wants this great sweater?

00:05:40.868 --> 00:05:42.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:47.868 --> 00:05:50.801
Come on down!

00:05:50.801 --> 00:05:52.267
Yes, come over here.

00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:54.267
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:58.801 --> 00:06:01.400
Welcome!

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:06.634
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:06.634 --> 00:06:08.901
This is it.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.400
This is it.
What is your name?

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.133
-Tori.
-Tori, where are you from?

00:06:12.133 --> 00:06:15.267
-I'm from Boston.
-From Boston! We love Boston!

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:16.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:16.934 --> 00:06:19.167
It does get
a little chilly in Boston,

00:06:19.167 --> 00:06:20.934
so this will go perfect.

00:06:20.934 --> 00:06:24.901
Are you a cow-- Do you like
country and being a cowboy?

00:06:24.901 --> 00:06:26.200
-I guess I do now.
-Yes, of course.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:27.234
-Yeah.
-Yeah, it's yours now.

00:06:27.234 --> 00:06:28.701
Would you like to try it on?

00:06:28.701 --> 00:06:29.801
We'd love to, yeah.

00:06:29.801 --> 00:06:30.868
I think there might be
one more button.

00:06:30.868 --> 00:06:32.567
-Yeah, one more button.

00:06:32.567 --> 00:06:33.667
-I think this is
going to be great.

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:35.100
You can't wear the hat.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:38.300
No, the hat is just decoration.
You don't wear the hat.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.033
Oh, whoa, whoa. This is subtle.

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:42.534
Are you kidding me?
Are you joking?

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:46.133
That is phenomenal.
Look at that!

00:06:46.133 --> 00:06:49.234
Look at that hat on the back.
That's unbelievable.

00:06:49.234 --> 00:06:51.000
It looks gorgeous.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.200
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.334
Congratulations.

00:06:53.334 --> 00:06:54.567
Give her a
round of applause, everybody.

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:56.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

